+"""REINFORCE with a sampler-centered score, plus optional importance-sampling
+corrections.
+
+Each token's score s_y = grad log p(y|h) is replaced by s_y - s_bar(h), with
+s_bar(h) = sum_v q(v|h) grad log p(v|h) the score's mean under the sampler q.
+On-policy (q = p) s_bar = 0 and nothing changes; under a sampler/trainer
+mismatch it removes the drift E_q[A|h] * s_bar(h) from the expected update
+(see REPORT.md). q is read from the sampler's top-k logprobs; its tail is
+modelled as proportional to p, which contributes no gradient.
 
 Every correction is REINFORCE with a detached weight w(r) on the ratio
 r = p/q of trainer (p) to sampler (q) probabilities, per token or per
